course: dictionary
lesson: 5233
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The context shows you which meaning the writer wants. «Today jet planes cross an ocean in a few hours» tells you a jet is an aircraft, because planes and crossing an ocean are about flying.
explain: In «air jets with cameras pick out the plastics», the words sorting plant and pick out tell you the jet is something moving air. Here a jet is a strong, narrow stream of air pushed out of a small hole. Always ask: what is this thing doing? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the same word is a different part of speech. In «while they jet away», jet is a verb, and the animal moves off quickly. «Jet-black» is another kind of word again: it describes something as very dark black.
fact: A word can have several meanings, and the context shows which one is right.
fact: A jet is a fast aircraft with jet engines.
fact: A jet is a strong, narrow stream of water, gas or air pushed out of a small hole.
fact: To jet off means to travel somewhere by plane; it is an informal verb.
fact: Jet is also a hard black stone used in jewellery, and «jet-black» means very dark black.
exercise: «Today jet planes cross an ocean in a few hours.» What is a jet in this sentence? | *A fast aircraft | A hard black stone | A stream of water from a hose | A wet day
exercise: «In a sorting plant, air jets with cameras pick out the plastics.» What is an air jet here? | A hard black stone | *A strong, narrow stream of air pushed out of a small hole | A type of jewellery | A fast aircraft
exercise: What does «jet-black» mean? | Very light grey | *Very dark black | Shiny like glass | Hot to touch
test: «Octopuses, squid and cuttlefish squirt ink to hide, while they jet away.» In this sentence, what does jet away mean? | *To move off quickly | To cook in ink | To sleep quietly | To travel somewhere by plane
test: «Volcanic ash can melt inside jet engines.» In this sentence, what does jet mean? | A stream of water from a hose | A hard black stone | Very dark black | *Part of a fast aircraft
exam: «The 2010 eruption grounded most flights across Europe, because volcanic ash can melt inside jet engines.» What does jet engine mean here? | A stream of water pushed from a hole | A hard black stone used in jewellery | A dark colour like jet-black | *An engine on a fast aircraft that pushes it forwards
